# Changelog updates

On any meaningful project change, update `changelog.md` in the repository root.

## Format

- Notation: [Keep a Changelog 1.1.0](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/)
- Versioning: [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html)
- Template: `rules/templates/changelog.md` (copy to the repo root when creating a project). Lives in a separate repository: https://gitlab.centrofinans.ru/devops/empty-project
- Section headers — English only (`Added`, `Changed`, `Removed`, `Fixed`)
- Entry text — **English only**

## When to update

Add an entry under `## [Unreleased]` when the change:

- adds, changes, or removes functionality
- fixes a bug
- changes API behavior, configuration, protocols, or deploy artifacts

Do not add: behavior-neutral refactors, comment typo fixes, purely internal edits with no user-facing effect.

## Categories

| Section  | When to use                    |
|----------|--------------------------------|
| Added    | New functionality              |
| Changed  | Existing behavior changed      |
| Removed  | Functionality removed          |
| Fixed    | Bug fix                        |

## Entry rules

- One line per change, starts with `- `
- Past tense or verb-led: “Added…”, “Fixed…”
- Concrete: what changed and who it matters to
- Related edits — one entry; unrelated — separate entries

## Example

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

### Added

- Added a `/health` endpoint for service readiness checks

### Fixed

- Fixed empty-body handling in POST `/items`
```

## Release

When tagging `main`:

1. Rename `## [Unreleased]` to `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` following semver
2. Create a new empty `## [Unreleased]` section above it
3. Tag message — English, same rules as entries
